# secdns zone — one record per line:  <name>  <type>  <value>
#
# SecDeploy generates this file from the site topology (topology.toml): one A record per
# component, pointing at the address of the resource that hosts it. You can also hand-write
# it. Names may be short (relative to the zone domain) or full FQDNs; blank lines and
# '#' comments are ignored. Reload after editing: `kill -HUP <pid>` or the console button.

# name          type   value
seccert         A      10.0.0.5
secsso          A      10.0.0.5
secrouter       A      10.0.0.5
secagent        A      10.0.0.5
secchat         A      10.0.0.5
secrecorder     A      10.0.0.5
secllm          A      10.0.0.6
secdns          A      10.0.0.5

# TXT records are supported too (used later for SecCert DNS-01):
# _acme-challenge.secrouter   TXT   "example-validation-token"
